+## 1. Experience (What the user lives)
+
+### 1a. JTBD Context
+
+**When** S001 has produced one or more action proposals from an uploaded capture, the operator wants to inspect each proposal and explicitly confirm only the actions that are correct, **so that** S003 receives a deliberate, human-approved set of actions rather than acting on an extraction guess.
+
+Cross-reference: `E001-capture-review/epic.md` defines this epic as human-reviewed action capture. No `product-contract.md` or persona artifact exists in this workspace, so `operator` is a reversible working persona and this story claims no magic moments.
+
+The review begins after extraction, not after scheduling: S001 has suggested possible actions, but its output is still provisional. The operator needs to be able to assess a proposal before agreeing to it, rather than discovering later that an inferred action was treated as a commitment. Confirmation is therefore the explicit boundary between a candidate and an action that may enter the scheduling flow.
+
+The job is deliberately narrow. This story does not alter the proposal, schedule it, or decide when it should occur; those behaviors either belong to the upstream capture/extraction step or to S003. Its outcome is a trustworthy handoff state: a proposal is either still unconfirmed and excluded from scheduling, or deliberately confirmed and available to the next story. The operator may choose not to confirm a proposal without that choice being interpreted as confirmation or as a scheduling failure.
+
+### 1b. Primary User Story
+
+As an operator, I want to review extracted action proposals and confirm the ones I accept so that only human-approved actions can be scheduled.
+
+The critical interaction is a conscious confirmation, not merely viewing a proposal or progressing past a screen. The review surface must make the state legible before and after the action, so the operator can stop with confidence when a proposal looks wrong or incomplete. When several proposals are present, the operator's choice applies to the specific proposal selected; reviewing or confirming one must not silently approve the rest.
+
+### 1c. Felt Quality (How the user feels)
+
+| Surface | Entry emotional state | Target felt outcome | Banned feelings |
+|---------|----------------------|--------------------|-----------------|
+| Proposal review | Cautious because extraction may be wrong | In control: each proposal is legible and approval is deliberate | pressured, confused, tricked |
+| Confirmation result | Ready to hand work onward | Certain which actions have been approved and which remain unconfirmed | ambiguity, accidental commitment |
+
+### 1d. Magic Moments Tied to This Story
+
+No product contract exists in this workspace, so this story makes no magic-moment claim.
+
