+## 4. Adversarial Cases (What must NOT happen)
+
+| Condition | Must NOT happen | Probe used to verify |
+|-----------|-----------------|----------------------|
+| A proposal arrives from S001 | It is silently treated as confirmed | Open the review surface before operator action and assert its state is unconfirmed |
+| The operator leaves a proposal unconfirmed | S003 can schedule it | Attempt the S003 handoff and assert the proposal is absent from confirmed actions |
+| The operator confirms one proposal among several | Other proposals are confirmed as a side effect | Confirm one proposal and assert all others remain unconfirmed |
+| The confirmation action is unavailable or fails | The UI implies that confirmation succeeded | Trigger the failure and assert the proposal remains unconfirmed with a clear retryable state |
+
+---
+
+## 5. Failure-Modes Handled
+
+| Dependency | Failure mode | Behavior | Verified by |
+|------------|--------------|----------|-------------|
+| S001 proposal output | No proposals are available | The review surface makes the empty state clear and offers no confirmation to perform | agent-LARP empty-state walkthrough |
+| Confirmation persistence | Confirmation cannot be saved | The proposal remains unconfirmed; the operator receives a clear failure state and may retry | agent-LARP failure injection |
+| S003 handoff | Downstream scheduling is unavailable | A successfully confirmed proposal remains confirmed; the operator is not told it has been scheduled | agent-LARP downstream-unavailable walkthrough |
+
