+## 7. Performance + Non-Functional Targets
+
+- Performance: The review surface must show the available proposal states before the operator decides; no project performance default exists in this workspace.
+- Accessibility: The proposal state and confirmation outcome must be perceivable without relying only on color.
+- Security/privacy: Confirmation is an explicit operator action; no unconfirmed proposal may cross the S003 boundary as confirmed.
+- Observability: Confirmation success and failure must be distinguishable in the runtime evidence required by this story.
+
+---
+
+## 8. Data + API (Last, not first)
+
+### Key Entities
+- **Proposal**: An action candidate produced by S001, with an unconfirmed or confirmed review state.
+- **Confirmed action**: A proposal explicitly accepted by the operator and eligible for S003 scheduling.
+
+### API Surface (if any)
+- **Proposal confirmation interface**: Records an explicit operator confirmation and exposes confirmed actions to S003; implementation details belong in `plan.md`.
